      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "4a7bddaf15ceb6d4fbe9e54cef4e2cf23a98263f",
            "subject": "LU-18746 flr: allow merge stale mirror"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-11 04:28:40.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-10-21 18:20:20.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20727 target: don't dealloc grant the export no longer has",
        "message": "LU-20727 target: don't dealloc grant the export no longer has\n\nAn OSC that idled out keeps its old grant and goes on\nspending it on DIO pages, which is a client bug (LU-19445),\nbut on reconnect the server grants the new export only one\nchunk. Writes then claim more grant than the export holds.\nAs with any such over-claim, tgt_grant_check() takes what\nthe export has and covers the rest from space not granted\nto any export, or fails the pages with ENOSPC.\n\nWhen a write fails after grant was allocated to its reply,\nthe whole amount was taken back from the export. Meanwhile,\nconcurrent writes from the same client may have consumed\nthat grant, so ted_grant and tot_granted went negative\nand the next RPC hit the LBUG in tgt_grant_incoming().\nsanity-quota test_58 on ZFS does exactly this: its mirror\nresync sends a burst of DIO RPCs after the OSC import\nidled out, and they fail with EDQUOT.\n\nTake back no more than the export still holds, so a bad\nclaim from any client cannot crash the server. Also inflate\nthe amount for clients without GRANT_PARAM, whose reply\ngrant was deflated after it was allocated.\n\nFixes: df2b5d99ad (\"LU-17933 target: do not break grants on RPC failure\")\nTest-Parameters: fstype=zfs testlist=sanity-quota env=ONLY=58,ONLY_REPEAT=20\nTest-Parameters: fstype=zfs mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=sanity-quota env=ONLY=58,ONLY_REPEAT=20\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ieadf12899e8ecd5f3a70bed2a5c594191a12e761\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
